artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "britpop": {"genre": "britpop", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "Britpop is a subgenre of alternative rock that originated in the United Kingdom. Britpop emerged from the British independent music scene of the early 1990s and was characterised by bands influenced by British guitar pop music of the 1960s and 1970s. The movement developed as a reaction against various musical and cultural trends in the late 1980s and early 1990s, particularly the grunge phenomenon from the United States. In the wake of the musical invasion into the United Kingdom of American grunge bands such as Nirvana.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Coldplay", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Oasis", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Radiohead", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Beatles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "classic rock": {"genre": "classic rock", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "Classic rock was originally conceived as a radio station programming format which evolved from the album oriented rock (AOR) format in the early-1980s. In the United States, this rock music format now features a large playlist of songs ranging from the 1960s, 1970s, 1980s and early 1990s, with some stations including a limited number of current releases.\n\nThe classic rock stations recreate the sound of Album Oriented Rock (AOR) stations of the 60s-90s (although usually with a much more limited playlist) and appeal mainly to adults.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "David Bowie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Pink Floyd", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Queen", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Beatles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "dance-pop": {"genre": "dance-pop", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "Dance-pop is a style of electronic dance music and a subgenre of pop music that evolved from Disco, circa 1981, that combines dance beats with a pop/R'n'B song structure. Because there is such an emphasis on fully-formed songs in dance-pop, it's often viewed as a separate classification unto itself apart from pure dance. Dance-pop is also closely related to the teen pop and Eurodance movements in the mid-1980s and late 1990s, the rise of boy bands and girl groups, and the reintroduction of the vocoder and similar such innovations.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "aespa", "streams": 68669, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 22193, "best_position": 60}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": 17570, "best_position": 87}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electronic": {"genre": "electronic", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "Electronic music refers to music that emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 26388, "best_position": 47}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 22193, "best_position": 60}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Eminem", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "aespa", "streams": 68669, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 22193, "best_position": 60}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "IU", "streams": 80836, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BLACKPINK", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bigbang", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Eminem", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "j-pop": {"genre": "j-pop", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "J-pop (\u30b8\u30a7\u30a4\u30dd\u30c3\u30d7 \"jeipoppu\"), an abbreviation for Japanese pop, is a musical genre that entered the musical mainstream of Japan in the 1990s.  Modern J-pop has its roots in 1960s music, such as The Beatles, and replaced kay\u014dkyoku (\"Lyric Singing Music,\" a term for Japanese pop music from the 1920s to the 1980s) in the Japanese music scene.  The term was coined by the Japanese media to distinguish Japanese music from foreign music, and now refers to most Japanese popular music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Red Velvet", "streams": 18157, "best_position": 84}, {"artist": "Kenshi Yonezu", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lisa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mitski", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Official HIGE DANdism", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "RADWIMPS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "TWICE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Vaundy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "YOASOBI", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "\u30e8\u30eb\u30b7\u30ab", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "kr", "country_name": "South Korea", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "RESCENE", "streams": 220063, "best_position": 3}, {"artist": "Hearts2Hearts", "streams": 193002, "best_position": 17}, {"artist": "IU", "streams": 80836, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "KiiiKiii", "streams": 80343, "best_position": 13}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": 75704, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "aespa", "streams": 68669, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "CORTIS", "streams": 67211, "best_position": 4}, {"artist": "NewJeans",